    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "50e2821a_a46dc13f",
        "filename": "src/effects/imagefilters/SkLightingImageFilter.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 231,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-20T19:48:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In combination with the CPU-side logic to choose the edgeBounds (either requiredInput, in which case this is a no-op, or the desired output edge, in which case the coords that have +/-1 added to them are clamped), this handles the new boundary condition behavior that sort of matches the SVG spec and handles the decal/affects-transparent-black behavior that works better with Skia\u0027s layering model.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 231,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 231,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "c87a437d219bc69740688bc7be211f330730bb31",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9eb7f56b_a4a10431",
        "filename": "src/effects/imagefilters/SkLightingImageFilter.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 246,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-20T19:48:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/effects/imagefilters/SkLightingImageFilter.cpp;drc\u003df24283f9968056c3b8e0a28bd91e615f25a15c8c;l\u003d1882\n\nAlso, this is the primary source of reduced performance in the CPU implementation now. Previously, the normal calculation would shift the sampled matrix around and read only the new values required: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/effects/imagefilters/SkLightingImageFilter.cpp;drc\u003df24283f9968056c3b8e0a28bd91e615f25a15c8c;l\u003d91.  If needed, and once the normal map is extracted into a cacheable stage, we could revisit such a CPU implementation outside of SkSL if we need to recover that performance.",
